<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="administrations">
    <teiHeader>
        <fileDesc>
            <titleStmt>
                <title>Presidential Administrations covered by the Foreign Relations of the United
                    States series</title>
            </titleStmt>
            <publicationStmt>
                <publisher>Office of the Historian, U.S. Department of State</publisher>
                <p>Controlled vocabulary for the administration coverage of FRUS volumes. Every
                    FRUS volume (frus-tei) classifies itself against this taxonomy via
                    <gi>keywords</gi> with <att>scheme</att>
                    <val>#frus-administration-coverage</val> in its
                    <gi>profileDesc</gi>/<gi>textClass</gi>.</p>
            </publicationStmt>
            <sourceDesc>
                <p>Administration identifiers match the term values used in the volume headers of
                    the FRUS v2 corpus. Display names, term-of-office dates, and portrait images
                    follow the reference implementation of the Historical Documents landing page
                    (hsg-shell, pages/historicaldocuments/index.xml).</p>
                <p>Encoding conventions: one <gi>category</gi> per administration identifier, in
                    chronological order; one <gi>catDesc</gi> per presidency, so a combined
                    administration such as <val>nixon-ford</val> carries two entries. Each
                    <gi>catDesc</gi> holds the display <gi>term</gi>, a coverage
                    <gi>date</gi> (the year range shown on the landing page, following the
                    reference implementation), a term-of-office <gi>date</gi> (shown in the
                    administration page heading), and a portrait <gi>ptr</gi>. The combined
                    nixon-ford category additionally carries a <gi>catDesc</gi> with
                    <att>n</att>=<val>combined</val> holding the joint heading label. A category without a portrait
                    (such as <val>pre-truman</val>, a coverage catch-all rather than a single
                    administration) is not shown in administration listings.</p>
            </sourceDesc>
        </fileDesc>
